## Feature Ablation

C/D features were removed to determine whether the engineered behavioral
features provided independent signal.

| Model | PR-AUC | ROC-AUC |
|---|---:|---:|
| Full 52-feature LightGBM | **0.5046** | **0.8992** |
| Without C/D features | 0.2395 | 0.8390 |
| Without C/D + engineered features | 0.2116 | 0.8366 |

The experiment showed that the anonymized C/D features contain substantial
predictive information. The current engineered features did not recover
that signal and therefore are not claimed as an improvement.

## M1 Conclusion

M1 establishes the real-data fraud detection benchmark for ORION³.

The IEEE-CIS dataset provides the benchmark for fraud-ranking capability.
The next stage will introduce an interpretable authorized-payment scam
simulator containing behavioral, message and receiver-network signals.
